  "[action] Wang Lung works the soil with his sons.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, I did not want to be made an officer, for it is a place for idle men who sit in their houses and do nothing, and I have no wish to be idle and to be made a fool of before men who are not worth my thinking of.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Is that a lie?\"",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung questions his son's statement.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung observes his son's behavior.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"But I have seen you at the great gate of the town and I have seen you come and go on horseback.\"",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"But have you not told me you are to be an officer?\"",
  "[action] The second son stands silently.",
  "[action] The eldest son laughs at his father.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"It is a lie, and I do not wish to be an officer, and I will not be an officer, and I will not be idle and sit in my house and be a fool.\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son laughs at his father.",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung argues about the official position.",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son laughs and leaves.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"There is no truth in what he said, for I was in the city only once and saw the court and the great men and how they wore their clothes. I did not dare to go in.\"",
  "[action] The eldest son laughs and leaves.",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing.",
  "[action] Wang Lung looks at his son.",
